    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678-a4">

                <pb facs="1082" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg946"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No. 222.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Margron.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 16, 1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 96.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor, in reply to your dispatch
                    of this date, wherein I am invited to name members of a commission to make an
                    inventory on the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Haytian Republic</hi>, to
                    inform you that such vessel being held by the Haytian authorities as a “good
                    capture,” that notwithstanding the case has been referred to the Department of
                    State at Washington, the custody of the vessel is in the hands of her captors,
                    who, according to law, are to take proper care of her. In consequence, I can not
                    accept to take part in any proceedings whatever, and beg most respectfully to
                    reiterate that the authorities holding such vessel are directly responsible to
                    the United States Government for any damages in the premises.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, I pray you, the assurance of my distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. W.
                            Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
